  "stdout": "{\"body\":\"Deferred from #312 batch 3 (registry mints).\\n\\n`data/ingredients/mapped/Cooked_Meat_Medium.yaml` is Robertson's cooked meat medium (MediaDive ingredient 1824, complex compound; Oxoid CM0081), a formulated anaerobe medium. Its identifier is `FOODON:03305103 \\\"meat (cooked)\\\"`, a food, from a 2026-05-01 `fuzzy-top` auto-upgrade: the medium was grounded to one of its parts. The verified correction (Section 3 step 3 / Section 6): mint `kgmicrobe.ingredient:cooked_meat_medium` with `FALLBACK_REGISTRY` and no FOODON identity, close or broad row, the `Artificial_Sea_Salt` shape.\\n\\nIt cannot land yet. Two mixtures reference the food through this record:\\n\\n- `Modified_Cooked_Meat_Medium.yaml` and `Fastidious_Anaerobe_Broth_With_Meat_Granules.yaml` each carry `components[0] = {component_name: \\\"meat (cooked)\\\", component_id: FOODON:03305103, reference_scope: MIM_CATALOG}`. Once no active record holds FOODON:03305103, `qc-component-partonomy` (required) fails with `UNRESOLVED_MIM_REFERENCE`, and the right fix is `reference_scope: EXTERNAL_TERM` (the part *is* the FOODON food term).\\n- But both mixtures are pinned byte-for-byte: `reports/semantic_review_20260921/resolution/components/dispositions.tsv` (`SEM:6028aad55b495239163c`, `current_record_sha256`) makes `build_review.py` fail with `Stale component disposition`, and `reports/sssom_completion_20260921/mapping_review/nonmapping_cohorts.json` carries SUPPORTED approvals for their registry rows keyed to the owner hash, which `assemble_review.py` refuses to restamp.\\n\\nSame family as #740 (identity-plan pin) and #745 (position-bound holds): a completed review pins records so that a later, verified, unrelated correction cannot be applied. Needed: a supersedable link for component-scope changes on the resolution side (the `mapping_changes/` receipts already do this for the completion side), and the assembler should withhold, not raise, when a cohort-approved owner is touched by a receipt.\\n\\nUntil then the record and the two component references stay as they are; `SOURCE_LABEL_IDENTIFIER_OVERRIDES` entries for the two \\\"Cooked meat medium\\\" source labels should be added with the mint.\\n\\nRelated: #312, #740, #745, #710.\",\"comments\":[],\"number\":748,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Cooked_Meat_Medium keeps FOODON:03305103 (the food) as its identity: the mint is blocked by two mixtures whose component references are pinned by the resolution component ledger\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-23T03:40:40Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/748\"}\n",
  "stderr": ""
}
